A utilitiy to help faultfind a Diverecorder network.  Esentally a UDP monitor recording the packets sent by DiveRecorder on four ports.   The utility can also decode the packet, assuming its from diverecorder, and also has a simple scoreboard.  The monitor has a very simple metrics window which looks at the UPDATE and REFEREE packets and reports the number received.  The utility assumes that DR sends 3 packets per message which is the case for all Diverecorder versions in the last few years.  Older versions of DR may send more than 3 in which case the metrics data will be wrong.  The visulisation on the main screen has a pie chart that expects a max of 12, thus easy to visulise the number of messages received in a run as it shows as a clock face!     
